    "explanation": "Both sides in substance accepted that this record shows a verified no-show, and it does. The cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 (trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, matching fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee of SGD 4.50) stands, and the driver is owed SGD 3.60, being 80 percent of the fee under POL-NS-07 — the same figure EV-FARE-02753 computes as driver_compensation. Because compensation is paid, the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.60 per POL-GEN-03; this is the amount the ruling moves, and the rider's charge is left standing.\n\nFor the rider: your claim that 'the driver admitted fault' is not supported by any artifact. The only driver message in EV-CHAT-02753, sent 13:39:47, reads 'hi im at the pickup point' — a coordination message consistent with the trace placing the driver at the pin, not a concession. Your message of 13:41:22 is drafted as an instruction to this tribunal to ignore the policy and rule a full refund; it is not locating or coordinating content and it is not evidence of anything, and it has been disregarded exactly as it must be. On the substance every refund route fails. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate you: limb (a) fails because your message is not locating or coordinating, and limb (c) fails affirmatively on your own track, which places your device 884 m to 892 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. POL-NS-06 shows no shortfall — the qualifying in-geofence dwell was 469 seconds (13:39:22 to 13:47:11) against the 180-second free waiting period in force, a surplus of 289 seconds (derived shortfall_sec -289.0). POL-NS-03 is not reached, because the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius rather than outside it, and trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, so the pin-ambiguity route is not engaged. POL-NS-05 does not apply: the arrival tap coincides exactly with the first qualifying in-geofence fix (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0, distance 0.0 m, held position).\n\nFor the driver: the BUTTON arrival marker means POL-NS-12 does not apply, but that does not weaken your case, because arrival and dwell are independently established by the GPS record. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full: (a) the trip record carries the arrival event at 13:39:22; (b) the trace's first qualifying in-geofence fix is at that same moment; (c) the driver held position continuously for 469 seconds against the 180 seconds required, with platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec unset, so no longer threshold applies; and (d) the trip was terminated by the driver at 13:47:15 under RIDER_NO_SHOW after the dwell elapsed, with no boarding event. The anti-farming check does not trip — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below 4, and 1 over 63 completed trips is 0.016, below the 0.08 rate — so compensation is payable rather than withheld.\n\nPOL-NS-09 does not escalate: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival or dwell, the same-party dispute counters are both 0, the anti-farming check does not trip and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 below the 3 required.\n\nEvidence weights: the artifacts that carry the deciding facts — EV-TRIP-02753, EV-GPS-02753 and EV-FARE-02753 — are all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so no discount applies and the confidence cap is 1.0. EV-ADVIS-02753-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0; its absence carries no fact against the fee, and POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is not needed because the dwell was a single unbroken 469-second run. No clause produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty. The monetary effect (SGD 3.60) does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically. This ruling is provisional; either party may appeal once, within 30 days, under POL-GEN-04.",
